messages.content:
An AI coding agent finished its turn and went idle. Below is its last message (Czech or English). Decide whether the human user must do something now.

needs_user = "yes" when anything in the message is left for the user, anywhere in the message, even if the rest is a finished report or the agent also waits for another agent:
- a question to the user, direct or indirect, also inside a list or in the middle of the text;
- a choice, decision, confirmation or approval the user has to make;
- questions or decisions from earlier that are still open ("otázka z minula pořád platí", "tvoje otázky jsou pořád otevřené", "open items", "Otevřené zůstává");
- a decision explicitly left to the user ("rozhodnutí je na vás/tobě", "je to na tobě", "your call");
- proposed changes or a plan that was not applied and waits for approval ("zatím jsem nic neaplikoval", "mám to provést?", "čekám na tvé potvrzení");
- an instruction or request for the user to do something (connect, run, provide, check, fix access, restart);
- an obstacle the agent cannot remove itself (missing access or permission, denied command, unavailable service, missing file or credential).

needs_user = "no" only when nothing at all is left for the user: a finished report or answer, or the agent only waits for another agent's reply. A generic closing offer ("Pokud chceš, můžu ...", "If you want, I can ...") with no pending decision is "no".
If unsure, answer "yes".

state = the main reason: needs_user (something for the user), blocked (an obstacle the agent cannot remove), waiting_agent (waits only for another agent), done (nothing left for anyone).

Answer only with JSON: {"needs_user": "yes"|"no", "state": "<label>"}.
